}
```

## UI Patterns

When displaying APA data in Blazor pages:

1. **Check database first** for static/semi-dynamic data
2. Show "Last updated: X hours ago" timestamp
3. Provide "Refresh" button for manual sync
4. Show loading indicator during sync
5. Handle offline scenarios gracefully (show cached data with warning)

## Summary

- **ConnectAPA**: API client library, no database logic
- **CueConnect757**: Contains sync services, database mapping
- **Cache aggressively**: Use database for reference data
- **Sync on-demand**: Let users control when to refresh
- **Live data**: Fetch directly from API when needed

# GraphQL Types

public sealed class GraphQlRequest
{
    public string OperationName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Query { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public object? Variables { get; set; }
}

public sealed class GraphQlResponse<T>
{
    public T? Data { get; set; }
    public GraphQlError[] Errors { get; set; } = [];
}

public sealed class GraphQlError
{
    public string Message { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

# PublicApaClient Requirements

public class PublicApaClient
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public PublicApaClient(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public Task<T> SendAsync<T>(string operationName, string query, object? variables);
    public Task<T[]> SendBatchAsync<T>(IEnumerable<GraphQlRequest> requests);
}

Rules:

- Do NOT attach Authorization header.
- Always send a JSON array of GraphQlRequest.
- Deserialize into GraphQlResponse<T>[].
- Throw exceptions on GraphQL errors or HTTP errors.
- Load queries from .graphql files under Public/Queries/.

# ApaClient (Authenticated) Requirements

public class ApaClient
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public string AccessToken { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public ApaClient(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public Task<T> SendAsync<T>(string operationName, string query, object? variables);
    public Task<T[]> SendBatchAsync<T>(IEnumerable<GraphQlRequest> requests);
}

Rules:

- Attach Authorization header.
- Wrap single requests into a one‑item batch.
- Deserialize as GraphQlResponse<T>[].
- Throw on GraphQL or HTTP errors.

# TestAPA.razor Usage Pattern

Copilot should generate Blazor code that:

- injects PublicApaClient
- loads the Southside league layout on initialization
- displays:
  - league name
  - divisions
  - teams in each division
  - schedule (dates only)
  - league news posts
- uses async OnInitializedAsync
- binds results to simple lists or tables
- uses strongly typed models from ConnectAPA.Models
- uses only public APA queries

Example pattern:

@inject PublicApaClient PublicAPA

protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
{
    var layout = await PublicAPA.GetLeagueLayoutAsync("Southside");
    Divisions = layout.Divisions;
    Schedule = await PublicAPA.GetScheduleAsync(Divisions.First().Id);
}

# Summary Rules

- Use HttpClient.
- Use System.Text.Json.
- Use https://gql.poolplayers.com/graphql.
- Use batched GraphQL payloads only.
- Load queries from .graphql files.
- PublicApaClient: no auth.
- ApaClient: requires bearer token.
- Do not mix public and authenticated queries.
- Do not add SQL or EF logic to ConnectAPA.